---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';

const company = 'Subliminal Design System LLC';
const address = '440 Monticello Ave Ste 1802 #625273, Norfolk, VA 23510, United States';
const email = 'support@subliminaldesignsystem.com';
const updated = 'November 11, 2026';

// The numbered sections below, in order, for the table of contents.
const sections = [
  { id: 'definitions', title: 'Definitions' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'why-we-use-it', title: 'Why we use it' },
  { id: 'who-we-share-it-with', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'international-transfers', title: 'International transfers' },
  { id: 'how-long-we-keep-it', title: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Security' },
  { id: 'your-rights', title: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'children', title: 'Children' },
  { id: 'do-not-track-and-global-privacy-control', title: '“Do Not Track” and Global Privacy Control' },
  { id: 'links-to-other-sites', title: 'Links to other sites' },
  { id: 'changes-to-this-policy', title: 'Changes to this Policy' },
  { id: 'contact-us', title: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy · Subliminal Design System"
  description="How Subliminal Design System LLC handles personal data on subliminaldesignsystem.com."
>
  <article class="policy">
    <header class="title-block">
      <h1 class="sds-text--title-huge">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="sds-text--content-large updated">Updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <h2 id="introduction" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">Introduction</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      This Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) explains how {company} (the “Company,” “we,” “us,” or
      “our”) processes Personal Data about people who visit subliminaldesignsystem.com (the “Site”)
      or contact us, and what rights you have. We act as the Controller of that Personal Data. We
      are based in the United States and the Site is available worldwide.
    </p>

    <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="toc">
      <h2 class="sds-text--title-xsmall">Table of contents</h2>
      <ol class="sds-text--interactive-medium">
        {sections.map((section) => (
          <li><a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="definitions" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">1. Definitions</h2>
    <ul class="sds-text--content-medium">
      <li>
        “Controller” means the person or organization that, alone or with others, decides the
        purposes and means of processing Personal Data.
      </li>
      <li>
        “Personal Data” means any information relating to an identified or identifiable person, such
        as a name, an email address, an IP address, or another online identifier.
      </li>
      <li>“You” means the person visiting the Site or contacting us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what-we-collect" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">2. What we collect</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site is a static documentation website. It has no accounts, no sign-up forms, and no
      payments. This is all we collect or store:
    </p>
    <ul class="sds-text--content-medium">
      <li>
        <strong>Standard request data.</strong> The Site is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare, Inc.
        When your browser loads a page, Cloudflare receives your IP address, browser and device
        information (the “user agent”), the page requested, the page that referred you, and the date
        and time. This is how every website is delivered, and it is also used to keep the Site secure
        and working.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you email {email}, we receive your email address,
        your name if you include it, and whatever you write.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One setting on your device.</strong> If you choose light or dark mode, your browser
        remembers it in local storage under the name <code>sds-mode</code>. It stays on your device,
        is not sent to us, and you can remove it by clearing the Site's data in your browser.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We do not currently use cookies, analytics, advertising or tracking tools, or fonts or scripts
      loaded from other companies, and we do not currently collect Personal Data through accounts
      or newsletters. If that changes, we will update this Policy before it does.
    </p>

    <h2 id="why-we-use-it" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">3. Why we use it</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We use Personal Data to deliver and secure the Site, and to read and reply to messages you
      send us. Where the law of your country requires a legal basis, ours is our legitimate interest
      in running a secure website and answering the people who contact us, which is not overridden
      by your data protection interests or fundamental rights. We collect Personal Data only where
      the processing is in our legitimate interests, where it is necessary to take steps you ask for
      (such as replying to you), where you consent, or where the law requires it. If we ever rely
      on your consent, you can withdraw it at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who-we-share-it-with" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We share Personal Data only with service providers that process it on our behalf and under
      their agreements with us: Cloudflare, Inc. (hosting, content delivery, and security for the
      Site) and Google LLC, through Google Workspace (to receive and send email). We may also disclose Personal Data
      where the law requires it, to protect our rights or the safety of others, or as part of a sale
      or reorganization of the business. <strong>We do not sell your Personal Data, and we do not
      share it for advertising across other companies' sites or apps.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2 id="international-transfers" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">5. International transfers</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We are in the United States, and our providers process data in the United States and in other
      countries where they operate. If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or
      Switzerland, your Personal Data may therefore be transferred outside your country. Where the
      law requires it, we rely on safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual
      Clauses, the UK Addendum, or a provider's certification under the Data Privacy Framework.
    </p>

    <h2 id="how-long-we-keep-it" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      Request data held by Cloudflare is kept for the period set out in Cloudflare's own policies.
      Emails you send us are kept for as long as we need them to respond and keep reasonable business
      records, and then deleted. Where there is no continuing need to retain Personal Data, we delete
      or aggregate it. If that is not possible, we store it securely and keep it apart from any
      further use until it can be deleted.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">7. Security</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We use appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect the Personal Data we
      process, designed to provide a level of security appropriate to the risk. The Site is served
      over HTTPS with strict security headers and does not load third-party scripts. If you have a
      concern about the security of your Personal Data, please contact us immediately.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-rights" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">8. Your rights</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of these rights over your Personal Data.
      We apply them to everyone, wherever you are, to the extent we can.
    </p>
    <ul class="sds-text--content-medium">
      <li>
        <strong>European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and Switzerland:</strong> to access your
        data, correct it, have it erased, restrict or object to its processing, receive a copy in a
        portable format, and withdraw consent at any time. You can also complain to your local
        data protection authority.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>California:</strong> to know what Personal Information we collect, use, and disclose;
        to delete it; to correct it; to opt out of its sale or sharing (we do neither); and not to be
        treated differently for using these rights.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Virginia and other US states with privacy laws:</strong> to confirm and access your
        Personal Data, correct it, delete it, obtain a copy, and opt out of targeted advertising,
        sale, and profiling (we do none of these). If we decline a request, you may appeal, and if
        the appeal is denied you may contact your state attorney general.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We may need to
      confirm your identity first, and we will respond within the time the law requires, normally 30
      to 45 days.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">9. Children</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect Personal Data
      from them. If you believe a child has sent us Personal Data, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="do-not-track-and-global-privacy-control" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">10. “Do Not Track” and Global Privacy Control</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      Because the Site does not track you across websites or use advertising or analytics tools,
      there is nothing for these browser signals to switch off, and we honor them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="links-to-other-sites" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">11. Links to other sites</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      The Site may link to other websites, such as code repositories. They have their own privacy
      practices, which this Policy does not cover.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">12. Changes to this Policy</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      We keep this Policy under regular review and may update this page at any time. The date at the
      top shows when it last changed. If we make a material change, we will say so clearly on the
      Site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact-us" class="sds-text--title-xsmall">13. Contact us</h2>
    <p class="sds-text--content-medium">
      If you have any question or concern about this Policy, contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, or write to:
    </p>
    <address class="sds-text--content-medium">
      {company}<br />
      {address}
    </address>
  </article>
</Layout>
